{
  "schema": "sdn-epm-canonical-preimage-vectors/1",
  "description": "EPM signing preimage conformance vectors (security audit SEC-038). Each vector is a minimal $EPM record carrying only LEGAL_NAME, ENTITY_TYPE (User) and SIGNATURE_TIMESTAMP; preimage_hex is the exact canonical signing payload, or error names why the record must be refused. Every implementation (Go node, hd-wallet JS, modules C++) must reproduce them byte for byte.",
  "rules": [
    "Signed strings are trimmed of ASCII space, TAB, LF, CR, VT and FF at both ends, and of nothing else; a field that trims to empty is omitted.",
    "Strings that are not valid UTF-8 are refused at signing and at verification.",
    "Serialization is RFC 8785 (JCS): keys sorted by UTF-16 code units; strings escape only quote, backslash, \\b, \\f, \\n, \\r, \\t and other bytes below 0x20 (lowercase \\u00xx); U+2028, U+2029, U+007F and all other characters are emitted raw.",
    "SIGNATURE_TIMESTAMP is written as an exact decimal integer."
  ],
